second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 244, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot (1982 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Escape 2000 and Blood Camp Thatcher) is a 1982 Australian dystopian action film directed by Brian Trenchard-Smith and starring Steve Railsback, Olivia Hussey, Michael Craig, and Lynda Stoner.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 245, \"end\": 346, \"text\": \"The cast is a mix of international actors, Australian soap opera actors and television personalities.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 347, \"end\": 648, \"text\": \"Widely considered an \\\"Ozploitation\\\" (or Australian exploitation film), the film is notable for its extreme violence and sadistic prison sequences, and it features plot elements of \\\"The Most Dangerous Game\\\", but rather than having human targets hunted for sport by a madman on his own island, the story\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 206, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot (2014 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Elimination Game) is a 2014 Australian dystopian futurist exploitation film directed by Jon Hewitt and co-written by Hewitt and his wife Belinda McClory.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 207, \"end\": 305, \"text\": \"Shot in Australia, the film stars Dominic Purcell, Viva Bianca, Robert Taylor and Belinda McClory.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 306, \"end\": 469, \"text\": \"Inspired by Brian Trenchard-Smith's 1982 \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\", the film features appearances by that film's Carmen Duncan, Roger Ward and the voice of producer Antony I.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 470, \"end\": 521, \"text\": \"Ginnane as television network head Charley Varrick.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 522, \"end\": 611, \"text\": \"In the near future, SEAL Commander Rick Tyler is sent to Libya to assassinate its leader.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 612, \"end\": 651, \"text\": \"After apparently completing the mission\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 588, \"text\": \"film ) 2 languages Cymraeg فارسی Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia 2014 Australian film Turkey Shoot Australian film poster Directed by Jon Hewitt Written by Belinda McClory Jon Hewitt Based on Turkey Shoot by Antony I.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02\", \"start\": 589, \"end\": 637, \"text\": \"Ginnane Brian Trenchard-Smith Produced by Antony\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"its colour and off-the-wall vitality , was released last year .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 167, \"text\": \"Perhaps a remake ( or “ re-invention ” , as director Jon Hewitt called it ) was doomed from the start .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 168, \"end\": 218, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot is many things ; imitable it is not .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 219, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"Explore more on these topics Film Rewatching classic Australian films Australian film reviews Share Reuse this content Comments ( … ) Sign in or create your Guardian account to join the discussion Most viewed Most viewed Film Books Music Art & design TV & radio Stage Classical Games News Opinion Sport Culture Lifestyle Original reporting and\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Brian Trenchard-Smith\", \"scope\": \"Director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"\", \"claim\": \"The 1982 Australian dystopian action film Turkey Shoot is directed by Brian Trenchard-Smith.\", \"answer\": \"Brian Trenchard-Smith\", \"quote\": \"Turkey Shoot (1982 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Escape 2000 and Blood Camp Thatcher) is a 1982 Australian dystopian action film directed by Brian Trenchard-Smith and starring Steve Railsback, Olivia Hussey, Michael Craig, and Lynda Stoner.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"scope\": \"Director of the 2014 film Turkey Shoot\", \"claim\": \"The 2014 Australian dystopian futurist exploitation film Turkey Shoot is directed by Jon Hewitt.\", \"answer\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"quote\": \"Turkey Shoot (2014 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Elimination Game) is a 2014 Australian dystopian futurist exploitation film directed by Jon Hewitt and co-written by Hewitt and his wife Belinda McClory.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {